      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This “Closing Prayer” for New Year’s Day was adapted by Mordecai Kaplan and Eugene Kohn from a prayer first published by unnamed “Members of the Faculty” of the Colgate-Rochester Divinity School (<tei:hi rend="italic">The Colgate-Rochester Divinity School Bulletin</tei:hi>, “Prayers for the New Year,” vol. 19 no. 2 (1947), pp. 65-71). Kaplan &amp; Kohn’s adapted prayer essentially contains excerpts from the prayer of the Faculty (excluding any with explicit Christian content). The adapted prayer was published in <tei:hi rend="italic">The Faith of America: Readings, Songs, and Prayers for the Celebration of American Holidays</tei:hi> (Jewish Reconstructionist Foundation 1951), p. 25-26. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_34742_notes"/>
